Sval: letterbox only the browsers that have a tab, and attach to a window once

RFPHelper's _attachWindow watches every .browserStack in the window, and
the preloaded new-tab browser sits in one with no tab until a new tab
adopts it. _roundContentSize asks the browser's tab browser for its
container, so while a preload is still on its initial about:blank (which
_noLetterBoxingFor does not exempt), turning letterboxing on threw
"aBrowser.getTabBrowser() is null" from the resize observer. A browser
with no tab is skipped; TabOpen rounds the preload once a tab takes it.

kPrefResistFingerprinting is a prefix of kPrefLetterboxing, and pref
observers match by prefix, so one change to the letterboxing pref reaches
_handleLetterboxingPrefChanged twice. Each call attached the window again,
and _detachWindow disconnects only the last resize observer, so the
others kept rounding browsers after letterboxing was off. _attachWindow
skips a window it is already attached to.

mozilla-central's RFPHelper is unchanged in both places; no Bugzilla bug
covers either.

diff --git a/toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/RFPHelper.sys.mjs b/toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/RFPHelper.sys.mjs
index f82d7309e1..f04f555d13 100644
